SonarQube is a static code analysis tool that helps developers measure and improve the quality, security, and maintainability of source code.
It automatically analyzes code and identifies:
	• 🐛 Bugs
	• 🔒 Security vulnerabilities
	• ⚠️ Code smells (poor coding practices)
	• 📊 Code coverage from tests
	• 🔄 Duplicate code
	• 🏆 Quality metrics and technical debt


A Jenkinsfile is a text file that defines your CI/CD pipeline as code.
Instead of configuring jobs manually in the Jenkins UI, you write all the pipeline stages, steps, and logic in a Jenkinsfile and store it in your source code repository (Git).
Why use a Jenkinsfile?
	• Version-controlled along with application code
	• Easy to review through pull requests
	• Reusable and maintainable
	• Consistent pipelines across environments
	• Supports Pipeline as Code


